    </g>

    <rect x="0" y="185" width="800" height="15" fill="#071b26" />
    <line x1="0" y1="185" x2="800" y2="185" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="2" />
  </svg>
</section>

<!-- TIME DIFFERENCE MECHANICS -->
<section class="method-section" id="time-difference" aria-labelledby="time-diff-heading">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Time Difference Mechanics</p>
    <h2 id="time-diff-heading">Analyzing the 6-Hour Gap: BST vs EST</h2>
    <p>
      The difference between British Summer Time (BST, UTC+1) and Eastern Standard Time (EST, UTC-5) equals <strong>6 hours</strong>. Because BST is located in Western Europe and incorporates summer daylight saving (+1 hour relative to UTC), while EST sits on the North American East Coast at UTC-5, EST is 6 hours behind BST when both time zone rules apply.
    </p>
    <p>
      When it is 12:00 PM (Noon) in London, local time in New York or Toronto is 6:00 AM on the same calendar day. When it is 6:00 PM BST in the UK, it is 12:00 PM (Noon) EST in Eastern North America.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 700px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 600 180" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="600" height="180" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      <g transform="translate(120, 90)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="50" fill="#12455d" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="3" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-30" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="25" y2="0" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <text x="0" y="70" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">BST (UTC+1)</text>
      </g>
      <g transform="translate(300, 90)">
        <text x="0" y="8" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="28" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">→</text>
        <rect x="-45" y="-30" width="90" height="24" rx="12" fill="#1b536e" />
        <text x="0" y="-14" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="800" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">-6 HOURS</text>
      </g>
      <g transform="translate(480, 90)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="50" fill="#12455d" stroke="#8fd7ff" stroke-width="3" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="-20" y2="20" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-30" stroke="#8fd7ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <text x="0" y="70" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">EST (UTC-5)</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>UTC Offsets Breakdown</h3>
      <p>BST operates at UTC+1, while EST operates at UTC-5. Calculating the offset separation: (+1) - (-5) = 6 hours difference.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Spring & Autumn Shift Dynamics</h3>
      <p>Because the US and UK change clocks on different weeks in March and October/November, the gap narrows to 5 hours (BST vs EDT) during summer, or 5 hours during transition weeks.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Core Collaboration Window</h3>
      <p>With a 6-hour difference, the primary window for real-time collaboration spans 3:00 PM – 6:00 PM BST, matching 9:00 AM – 12:00 PM EST.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 24-HOUR CONVERSION TABLE -->
<section class="examples-section" id="conversion-chart" aria-labelledby="chart-heading">
  <div>
    <h2 id="chart-heading">Complete 24-Hour BST to EST Conversion Table</h2>
    <p>This reference chart maps every hour of British Summer Time (BST) directly to Eastern Standard Time (EST).</p>

