  <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common Pitfalls in BST to EST Conversions</h2>
  
  <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: var(--muted);">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Confusing BST with GMT:</strong> BST is UTC+1 (summer time), whereas GMT is UTC+0 (winter time). Using the wrong UK baseline leads to 1-hour scheduling errors.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Ignoring Spring/Autumn Shift Dates:</strong> The US and UK shift clocks on different Sundays in March and October/November. Double check offset during transition weeks.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Calendar Date Boundary Drops:</strong> 1:00 AM BST corresponds to 7:00 PM EST on the <em>previous day</em>. Keep track of calendar dates when converting overnight hours.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

